1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,603
Every to-do app assumes you have the same energy every day.

2
00:00:04,603 --> 00:00:10,943
For students living with chronic illness, ADHD, or depression, that just isn't true.

3
00:00:10,943 --> 00:00:15,774
On a bad day, the list doesn't shrink. It just turns into guilt.

4
00:00:16,388 --> 00:00:18,978
Spoonful is built on spoon theory.

5
00:00:18,978 --> 00:00:24,387
You get a limited number of spoons each day, and every task costs some.

6
00:00:24,387 --> 00:00:30,177
So Spoonful starts with one question: how much energy do you have right now?

7
00:00:30,793 --> 00:00:33,066
Here's a typical student week.

8
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:38,219
On a great day, Spoonful plans the must-dos and the deadlines first:

9
00:00:38,219 --> 00:00:43,600
the doctor's appointment, the email due today, even the big lab report.

10
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:46,707
And it always keeps one spoon in reserve.

11
00:00:47,315 --> 00:00:51,949
Same list. Rough day. Now only two things fit.

12
00:00:51,949 --> 00:00:56,483
Everything else is still here, with a reason:

13
00:00:56,483 --> 00:01:01,621
"Your energy is already spoken for. This can wait."

14
00:01:01,621 --> 00:01:04,039
No red badges. No shame.

15
00:01:04,643 --> 00:01:10,119
The lab report is due tomorrow, but 5 spoons will never fit a low day.

16
00:01:10,119 --> 00:01:15,204
So we break it down, with built-in suggestions that work offline.

17
00:01:15,204 --> 00:01:19,585
Now, on an okay day, Spoonful plans just the first step.

18
00:01:19,585 --> 00:01:22,167
The deadline still moves forward.

19
00:01:22,781 --> 00:01:26,369
Focus mode shows one thing at a time.

20
00:01:26,369 --> 00:01:28,988
Done. Not now. Or: too big?

21
00:01:28,988 --> 00:01:35,970
It can read each step aloud, and the gentle timer counts up, never down.

22
00:01:36,586 --> 00:01:38,867
Accessibility is built in:

23
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:44,570
larger text, dyslexia-friendly spacing, high contrast, dark mode,

24
00:01:44,570 --> 00:01:46,852
and full keyboard support.

25
00:01:46,852 --> 00:01:51,590
Our automated WCAG 2.1 AA audit finds zero violations.

26
00:01:52,207 --> 00:01:56,985
Under the hood, the planner is a pure, tested engine:

27
00:01:56,985 --> 00:02:01,313
16 unit tests plus a browser accessibility test.

28
00:02:01,313 --> 00:02:04,920
No server. No account. It works offline.

29
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:08,346
Your health data stays on your device.

30
00:02:08,952 --> 00:02:14,278
Spoonful. Plan by energy, not by hours.

31
00:02:14,278 --> 00:02:18,921
Try it: waazy-w.github.io/spoonful
